 "rulebook": "FIVB Official Volleyball Rules 2025-2028: Rule 1 (the court 18 m x 9 m, the attack lines), Rule 2 (the men's net, top at 2.43 m, the antennas), Rule 3 (the ball: 65-67 cm round, 260-280 g), Rule 8 (ball in and out: the lines belong to the court; a ball that touches an antenna or crosses outside the crossing space is out), Rule 9.2 (the hit: not caught or thrown, one contact), Rule 10.2 (the ball may touch the net), Rule 11.2-11.3 (the foot not wholly beyond the centre line; no contact with the net), Rule 13 (the attack hit)",
 "deviations": [
  "The set is a scripted launch from the setter's place at position 2/3: a ball without spin that rises to 4.5 m and comes down 0.5 m from the net at position 4, the same in every attempt, instead of a team-mate.",
  "The family asks for the spike, where Rule 13 allows any attack hit: the ball is struck with a hand (the parts beyond the wrist) at a point above the height of the net's top, while the robot is in the air in a jump (its pelvis rises at least 0.1 m above where it was when the feet left the floor: drawing the legs up is not a jump), after the ball has passed its highest point, and the ball leaves the hand moving downward and at least 1.0 times as fast as it arrived (a hand held in the ball's path returns it slower). 'Not caught or thrown' is a contact of at most 0.1 s.",
  "Rule 11 is judged for the whole attempt, until the robot has landed and stood for 1.0 s after the ball is down: there is no rally to end the play.",
  "No blockers or defenders, no wind."
 ],
 "texts": {
  "sentence": "Spike the set: jump and strike the volleyball that comes down near the net with a hand, above the height of the net, down into the opponent's court, and land on your feet without touching the net.",
  "rules": "You are the outside hitter on an official volleyball court (9.0 m by 9.0 m on each side of the net; the net's top 2.43 m high, an antenna above each side line). You stand on your attack line facing the net, which is 3.0 m ahead of you; the left side line is 1.0 m to your left. A volleyball (0.21 m across, 0.27 kg, in air) is set from your right 3.0 s after the start: it rises to 4.5 m and comes down 0.5 m from the net, in front of you. In order: (1) the spike: the ball's first contact after the set, before it touches the floor, is with a hand of yours (the parts beyond the wrist; one or both), after the ball has passed its highest point, at points that are all higher than the net's top, while you are in the air (nothing of you touches the floor or anything else) in a jump: during that flight your pelvis rises at least 0.1 m above the height it had when your feet left the floor. All contacts lie within 0.1 s (the strike is over when the ball has been clear of you for 0.03 s), and the ball leaves your hand moving downward and at least 1.0 times as fast as it was just before the hand touched it. (2) the ball crosses the net's plane above the net and between the antennas; it may touch the net. (3) the ball's first contact with the floor is in the opponent's court (9.0 m by 9.0 m, lines included); from then on the ball is dead and what it touches is not judged. (4) after that you stand for 1.0 s without a break (only your feet on the floor, your trunk within about 20 degrees of upright, your pelvis slower than 0.35 m/s): that is the success. You fail if the ball touches the floor before the spike, if any part of you other than a hand touches it, if you touch it before it has passed its highest point, from the floor, below the height of the net's top, or in a flight in which your pelvis did not rise 0.1 m, if the contacts last longer than 0.1 s, if the ball leaves the hand upward or slower than that, if you touch the ball again, if it crosses the net's plane under the net or outside the antennas or touches an antenna, if it lands anywhere else, if you touch the net, an antenna or a post at any time, if a foot of yours is on the floor wholly beyond the centre line, if you fall (your pelvis lower than 0.35 m above the floor, or any part of you other than the feet on the floor), or after 12 s. The ball cannot be gripped, and it cannot be touched while it waits to be set.",
  "venue": "You face the net (+x) from the attack line. The ball waits 2.3 m above the floor at the setter's place, 1 m from the net and 5 m to your right. About 3 s after the start it is set towards you along the net; it reaches 4.5 m and comes down at about 57 degrees below the horizontal and 6 to 7 m/s, still moving to your left. About 1.26 s after the set it is 2.8 m above the floor, 2.5 m ahead of where you stand and straight in front of you, half a metre from the net; about 0.07 s later it is down to the height of the net's top, and untouched it lands just outside the left side line.",
  "difficulty": "The robot reaches 2.24 m standing: its hand has to be above 2.43 m, so it must jump at least a quarter of a metre, after an approach of about 2 m on a walking policy, and swing through a ball that falls through the reachable window in under a tenth of a second, half a metre from a net it may not touch, then land a 67 kg body on its feet. No jumping skill is built in."
 },
